    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2SKeE4wKZPF1ypZ5N34wsv2)_\n\n## Merge order\n\n- Independent: touches only `sp-base-libraries` (code and doc).\n- Merge in any order; no PR depends on it and it depends on none.\n\n## What and why\n\n- `citar-open-entry` on a `.bib` file printed dozens of `Wrote ...~undo-tree~` lines, one per bibliography file, and slowed Emacs.\n- Likely writer: `lem-full-auto-save` in `sp-backups` runs `basic-save-buffer` on every modified file buffer after 5 idle seconds; `undo-tree` writes a history file on each save.\n- New `sp-undo-tree-skip-history-for-bib` sets `undo-tree-auto-save-history` to nil buffer-locally for `.bib` buffers.\n- It runs from `bibtex-mode-hook` and `find-file-hook`, so late mode setting is covered.\n- History for other files is unchanged.\n- Doc updated in `docs/tangles/base/sp-base-libraries.org` (bullets).\n- Not verified: `tools/check-tangle.sh` could not run in the cloud container (no Emacs). The `.el` block matches the doc block by hand.\n- Not done: finding why those `.bib` buffers are modified at all; this PR removes the cost, not that cause.\n\n## Testing checklist\n\n- [x] Reload `sp-base-libraries` (or restart Emacs).\n- [x] Run `citar-open-entry`; no `Wrote ...~undo-tree~` lines for `.bib` files.\n- [x] `~/.emacs.d/undo/` gets no new `.bib` files.\n- [x] Edit and save an `.org` file; its undo history is still written.\n- [ ] `M-x check-tangle` / `tools/check-tangle.sh` passes.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiAU5nbEWPqNx9ff4im)_",
